# AIROUTE UI & CSS RULES (CURRENT)

====================================================
## 1) Global CSS Safety (DO NOT BREAK)
====================================================

- NEVER modify these unless user explicitly asks:
  - `src/app/globals.css`
  - `tailwind.config.ts`

If UI looks broken:
1) inspect the actual component/page code first
2) apply minimal local Tailwind fixes
3) do not rewrite global styles

====================================================
## 2) Reuse Components (NO CLONING)
====================================================

- Reuse existing components from `src/components` whenever possible.
- Do NOT invent paths/components. Verify they exist.
- If you need a variation, extend via props (variant/size) instead of copy-pasting.

====================================================
## 3) UI-Lab
====================================================

- `/ui-lab` is internal playground.
- When you change shared UI components, update `/ui-lab` for visual check.
- Never link `/ui-lab` in public navigation.

====================================================
## 4) Mobile & Readability Defaults
====================================================

- Mobile-first readability is mandatory:
  - side padding: `px-4` or `px-5`
  - body text not smaller than `text-sm`
  - use `leading-relaxed` for paragraphs
- Keep UI simple: fewer badges, fewer micro-metrics.

====================================================
## 5) KR UI Tone (Workspace / B2B)
====================================================

- Prefer clear Korean labels.
- Big buttons, simple states.
- Status > settings.
- "결과가 곧 콘텐츠" (email content is the deliverable).
